# COMPONENT

## KnowledgeLake

### PACKAGE

org.simplemodeling.textus.knowledgelake

### STYLE

full-fledged-with-standalone

### SUMMARY

Logical Knowledge Lake Material access and explicit registration.

### DESCRIPTION

Knowledge Lake exposes logical Material search, metadata, original reads and
explicit registration commands through the caller's CNCF execution context.
Material references and resource selectors remain opaque to clients. Existing
read-only Operations operate independently of OpenClaw processing and never
initiate preparation. Registration commands require explicit registered mode
and owning-host admission; their declaration does not establish runtime availability.

> MATERIAL PACKAGE V1 NOTE FOR CODEX
>
> Material is now distinguished from PreparedMaterial.
> - Material: self-describing Knowledge Lake package, physically journaled, containing source/working assets and provenance.
> - PreparedMaterial: preparation result Entity used for candidate extraction, with the existing stronger lifecycle/version semantics.
> - KAR: PreparedMaterial transport/export artifact, not the Material package storage format.
>
> Design source: docs/notes/material-package-v1.md
>
> When native CML modeling is implemented, inspect current Cozy/CML grammar first and model Material / MaterialAsset / Provenance / lineage only with supported constructs. Do not invent syntax.

# SERVICE

## Material

### SUMMARY

Search and read authorized Materials, inspect registration status and explicitly register/materialize contributions.

### OPERATION

#### searchMaterials

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### ACCESS

###### POLICY

authenticated_only

##### SUMMARY

Return an authorized page of Material references and titles.

##### DESCRIPTION

Read-only, case-insensitive title/reference substring search. Text is at most
256 characters. Offset defaults to 0 and must be nonnegative; limit defaults
to 20 and must be between 1 and 100. Results use stable reference ordering.
Paging and hasMore apply after caller authorization without disclosing
unauthorized metadata. Empty results contain an empty items collection.

##### INPUT

###### VALUE

####### MaterialSearchQuery

######## EXTENDS

QueryAction

######## ATTRIBUTE

| name   | type   | multiplicity |
|--------|--------|--------------|
| text   | string | ?            |
| offset | int    | ?            |
| limit  | int    | ?            |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

MaterialSearchResult

#### getMaterial

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### ACCESS

###### POLICY

authenticated_only

##### SUMMARY

Resolve an opaque Material reference to authorized metadata.

##### DESCRIPTION

Accept the TKL-issued Material reference unchanged, including an existing
Knowledge Lake URN. Caller admission and Material read authorization precede
resource access. Return logical resources and attributed provenance without
exposing physical storage or connection details.
Optional evidenceResourceIds explicitly requests resource-scoped source-version
observations around complete original reads. Omission or an empty collection
retains metadata-only behavior. IDs must be distinct, at most 128, and each
nonempty and at most 256 characters without controls. Every original is resolved
under the caller before reading any selected original. Known unchanged versions
return available evidence; unknown versions remain unverified without revision.
Changed originals fail without partial observations, fallback or business writes.
An observation promises neither version-pinned access nor retention.

##### INPUT

###### VALUE

####### MaterialSelectionQuery

######## EXTENDS

QueryAction

######## ATTRIBUTE

| name                | type   | multiplicity |
|---------------------|--------|--------------|
| materialRef         | string | 1            |
| evidenceResourceIds | string | *            |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

MaterialMetadata

#### readOriginal

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### ACCESS

###### POLICY

authenticated_only

##### SUMMARY

Return one authorized logical original as a private binary response.

##### DESCRIPTION

Select the original using an opaque Material reference and its logical
resourceId. Caller authentication, Operation admission and Material/resource
read authorization precede connection lookup and outbound access. Return
original bytes with the admitted media type and private/no-store, nosniff,
sandbox and attachment headers. This read never initiates preparation or
registration and never substitutes another resource on failure.

##### INPUT

###### VALUE

####### OriginalSelectionQuery

######## EXTENDS

QueryAction

######## ATTRIBUTE

| name        | type   | multiplicity |
|-------------|--------|--------------|
| materialRef | string | 1            |
| resourceId  | string | 1            |

##### OUTPUT

###### VALUE

####### MaterialOriginalResult

######## EXTENDS

OperationResult

######## ATTRIBUTE

| name    | type | multiplicity |
|---------|------|--------------|
| content | blob | 1            |

#### createMaterialRegistration

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### ACCESS

###### POLICY

authenticated_only

##### SUMMARY

Persist a caller-authorized Prepared registration from one neutral contribution.

##### DESCRIPTION

Accept contribution as one complete textus.material-contribution/1 JSON value,
retaining all source/provenance/document JSON and Unicode. Exact registered mode,
an actual provider-authenticated caller and the owning host registration
configuration are required. Authorize the configured subject before contribution,
source or database access; validate bound source declarations locally without
credential or provider IO. TKL selects location/storage binding, derives native
principals and delegates native identity issuance and create authorization.
Return registrationId, positive committed revision, state prepared and the planned
materialRef only after durable native acknowledgement. The reference is unavailable
until registered; obtain logical metadata through getMaterial after that status.
No owner, URN, folder, connection, grant or destination is accepted from the caller.
Absent configuration is service-unavailable; invalid source correspondence is
argument-invalid. Native authorization/storage/uncertainty Conclusions propagate.
An unacknowledged create is unresolved: never automatically retry or deduplicate
by an App/business key. No provider read/write occurs. Result JSON projects
registration_id/material_ref and exposes no private contribution or provider data.

##### INPUT

###### VALUE

####### MaterialRegistrationCreateCommand

######## EXTENDS

CommandAction

######## ATTRIBUTE

| name         | type | multiplicity |
|--------------|------|--------------|
| contribution | json | 1            |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

MaterialRegistrationResult

#### getMaterialRegistration

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### ACCESS

###### POLICY

authenticated_only

##### SUMMARY

Inspect the actual native caller-authorized registration status without provider access.

##### DESCRIPTION

Accept registrationId as the exact native-issued registration EntityId, distinct
from the opaque Material URN, and validate its collection through native owner
support. Require actual provider authentication, explicit registered mode and
ordinary native read authorization. No registration/OAuth configuration or
provider access is required. Return registrationId, the positive observed
committed revision, actual state prepared/materializing/registered and assigned
planned materialRef. Only registered makes the Material available through ordinary
search/get/read; logical metadata then comes from getMaterial. Invalid selectors,
missing/unauthorized records and native load failures retain their structured
Conclusions. This query is the saved-status authority after uncertain commands;
it performs no writes, credential lookup, preparation or mutation replay and
does not authorize a retry. Result JSON uses registration_id/material_ref and
contains no contribution, physical mappings, permissions or provider grants.

##### INPUT

###### VALUE

####### MaterialRegistrationSelectionQuery

######## EXTENDS

QueryAction

######## ATTRIBUTE

| name           | type   | multiplicity |
|----------------|--------|--------------|
| registrationId | string | 1            |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

MaterialRegistrationResult

#### materializeMaterial

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### ACCESS

###### POLICY

authenticated_only

##### SUMMARY

Materialize one authorized Prepared registration after acknowledged native progress.

##### DESCRIPTION

Accept only registrationId, validated as the exact native registration EntityId
and collection through owner support. Require actual provider authentication,
explicit registered mode, owning host configuration, its allowed subject and
ordinary native authorization. Load/authorize the actual record and reject
non-Prepared state before private connection/provider access. Check retained
storageBinding/location against current configuration without rebinding old
records. Construct existing managed source/FileStore/writer capabilities without
IO; native write authorization and acknowledged durable Materializing using the
observed revision precede every external provider program. Execute the writer
once, then persist Registered with confirmed private mappings using the actual
returned Materializing revision. Return registrationId, positive committed
revision, state registered and materialRef only after confirmed native persistence.
Use getMaterial for logical metadata. Missing configuration is service-unavailable;
state conflicts are structured operation-conflict. Native authorization, mapping,
source/provider and save/uncertainty Conclusions propagate unchanged. A failure
may retain Materializing and remote bytes, or an uncertain final acknowledgement
may leave Registered. Inspect getMaterialRegistration for actual saved status;
never automatically replay, reset or delete output. Result JSON projects
registration_id/material_ref and contains no physical maps, credentials or grants.

##### INPUT

###### VALUE

####### MaterialRegistrationMaterializeCommand

######## EXTENDS

CommandAction

######## ATTRIBUTE

| name           | type   | multiplicity |
|----------------|--------|--------------|
| registrationId | string | 1            |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

MaterialRegistrationResult

## MaterialDelivery

### SUMMARY

TKL-owned mobile delivery discovery, preparation, original ingress and registration.

### DESCRIPTION

Additive mobile delivery contract defined by mobile-material-delivery-v1.md.
All Operations use the actual CNCF caller and ordinary native authorization.
The handwritten runtime enables this service with durable native checkpoints.
Controlled specifications do not establish live Google access or Android acceptance.

### OPERATION

#### getDestination

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### ACCESS

###### POLICY

authenticated_only

##### SUMMARY

Read the permitted logical destination without provisioning or provider IO.

##### DESCRIPTION

Return configurationRequired when the explicit server delivery configuration is absent. Production clients discover integration information here; test hosts may supply explicit configuration. Return no credential, physical folder or provider key. This declaration does not establish an implemented runtime.

##### INPUT

###### TYPE

void

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

MaterialDeliveryDestination

#### prepare

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### ACCESS

###### POLICY

authenticated_only

##### SUMMARY

Prepare one durable delivery for an immutable committed contribution.

##### DESCRIPTION

Preserve the structured contribution JSON including nulls and resource associations. Scope request correlation to the authenticated caller and application. Use ordinary native claim/load before remote effects; the same request must reconcile the same retained destination and delivery. A different contribution is a conflict. This declaration does not establish implemented persistence.

##### INPUT

###### VALUE

####### MaterialDeliveryPrepareCommand

######## EXTENDS

CommandAction

######## ATTRIBUTE

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------|------|--------------|
| requestId | string | 1 |
| contribution | json | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

MaterialDeliverySnapshot

#### findForRequest

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### ACCESS

###### POLICY

authenticated_only

##### SUMMARY

Find the caller-authorized delivery for the exact committed request.

##### DESCRIPTION

Return confirmed authorized absence distinctly from datastore or authentication failure. Do not disclose another caller delivery or initiate preparation, upload or registration.

##### INPUT

###### VALUE

####### MaterialDeliveryRequestQuery

######## EXTENDS

QueryAction

######## ATTRIBUTE

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------|------|--------------|
| requestId | string | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

MaterialDeliveryLookup

#### get

##### TYPE

QUERY

##### ACCESS

###### POLICY

authenticated_only

##### SUMMARY

Read actual retained delivery progress without provider mutation.

##### DESCRIPTION

Accept the opaque delivery reference unchanged. Require native read authorization. Return a Material reference only after confirmed registration; a planned URN or uploaded bytes are not registration.

##### INPUT

###### VALUE

####### MaterialDeliverySelectionQuery

######## EXTENDS

QueryAction

######## ATTRIBUTE

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------|------|--------------|
| deliveryRef | string | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

MaterialDeliverySnapshot

#### uploadOriginal

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### ACCESS

###### POLICY

authenticated_only

##### SUMMARY

Receive one declared binary original for the caller-authorized delivery.

##### DESCRIPTION

Use native binary input, not JSON text or base64. Authorize the retained delivery and declared resource before provider access. Validate media and length against its declaration. Retain confirmed progress; uncertain provider outcomes require reconciliation rather than an automatic new create. The generated blob decoder still needs ingress verification.

##### INPUT

###### VALUE

####### MaterialDeliveryUploadCommand

######## EXTENDS

CommandAction

######## ATTRIBUTE

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------|------|--------------|
| deliveryRef | string | 1 |
| resourceId | string | 1 |
| content | blob | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

MaterialDeliverySnapshot

#### finalize

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### ACCESS

###### POLICY

authenticated_only

##### SUMMARY

Register stored originals and metadata and return the actual Material reference.

##### DESCRIPTION

Require complete original and document associations. Preserve native registration identity and actual status across reply loss. Queries reconcile uncertain outcomes; do not replay the old one-shot materializer or issue another registration. Studio acknowledgement remains separate.

##### INPUT

###### VALUE

####### MaterialDeliveryFinalizeCommand

######## EXTENDS

CommandAction

######## ATTRIBUTE

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------|------|--------------|
| deliveryRef | string | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

MaterialDeliverySnapshot

#### prepareOriginalTransfer

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### ACCESS

###### POLICY

authenticated_only

##### SUMMARY

Prepare or inspect the retained direct-upload session without sending original bytes.

##### DESCRIPTION

Authorize the retained delivery owner. Preserve destination, route and per-original
provider session across restart. Unknown outcomes never select another route.

##### INPUT

###### VALUE

####### MaterialDeliveryDirectPrepareCommand

######## EXTENDS

CommandAction

######## ATTRIBUTE

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------|------|--------------|
| deliveryRef | string | 1 |
| resourceId | string | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

MaterialDeliveryTransfer

#### confirmOriginalTransfer

##### TYPE

COMMAND

##### ACCESS

###### POLICY

authenticated_only

##### SUMMARY

Independently confirm the notified direct-upload result before accepting the original.

##### DESCRIPTION

Authorize the retained delivery owner. Preserve destination, route and per-original
provider session across restart. Unknown outcomes never select another route.

##### INPUT

###### VALUE

####### MaterialDeliveryDirectConfirmCommand

######## EXTENDS

CommandAction

######## ATTRIBUTE

| name | type | multiplicity |
|------|------|--------------|
| deliveryRef | string | 1 |
| resourceId | string | 1 |
| transferRef | string | 1 |
| result | json | 1 |

##### OUTPUT

###### TYPE

MaterialDeliverySnapshot

